# Claim states

Every statement about work in this repository is in exactly one of these
states. Never use two at once and never let a later sentence quietly promote
one.

| State | Means | Minimum evidence |
|---|---|---|
| `PROPOSED` | Written down. Nothing has run. | The proposal itself. |
| `LAUNCHED` | Something was started. | The launch instrument and a stable locator for the thing started. |
| `OBSERVED` | Something was seen to happen. | The instrument, the observation time, and the raw output. |
| `READY_TO_COMMIT` | A work unit produced artifacts and stopped at its own boundary. | The artifacts plus a receipt manifest with per-file `sha256` and a `bundle_sha256`. |
| `RECONCILED` | The artifacts are in immutable remote custody. | The commit SHA plus a byte-for-byte read-back addressed by that SHA. |
| `ACCEPTED` | An independent party judged it against criteria it did not write. | An acceptance record naming an acceptor that is not the producing run. |

## What is not a state

A pull request is a projection. An archive is a projection. An
acknowledgement, a handover document and a status message are projections. A
provider reporting a run as finished is a **status**, not an acceptance. None
of these advances the claim state and none may be described as delivery,
completion or capability.

## Evidence labels

Label every factual claim exactly one of:

- `DIRECTLY_REPRODUCED` — you ran it in this runtime. Include the command and
  the observed output.
- `DOCUMENTED` — an official source says so. Include the URL. You did not run
  it.
- `HYPOTHESIS` — untested inference. It is not evidence of capability.

Never blur them and never let a `DOCUMENTED` capability be summarised as a
working one. A capability you could not test is not one you may present as
proven. When you could not test something, say what stopped you and name the
instrument that would settle it.

## Self-acceptance

A producing run may not accept its own work, and may not write a non-null
acceptor for itself. If acceptance has been requested and not granted, the
state is `REQUESTED_NOT_GRANTED` and stays there.
